pi&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Wildscape, Orkney","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":58.983668,"lo":-2.95768,"d":198,"h":"Mo-Fr 10:30-16:00; Sa 11:00-15:30"},{"n":"Town Hall","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":58.981635,"lo":-2.960769,"d":376},{"n":"Mercat Cross","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":58.981603,"lo":-2.960351,"d":378},{"n":"Orkney Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":58.981328,"lo":-2.961188,"d":413,"h":"Mo-Sa 10:30-12:30,13:30-17:00","w":"https://www.orkneymuseums.co.uk/our-museums/the-orkney-museum/","wp":"en:The Orkney Museum","ds":"The Orkney Museum, formerly Tankerness House Museum, is a history museum in Kirkwall, Orkney, Scotland. Run by Orkney Islands Council, the museum covers the history of the Orkney Islands from the Stone Age through the Picts and Vikings to the present day. The museum was founded in 1968 as Tankerness House Museum and in 1999 changed its name to The Orkney Museum.","wpu":"The Orkney Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Orkney_Museum_%28geograph_6172873%29.jpg/960px-Orkney_Museum_%28geograph_6172873%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bishop's Palace","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":58.980869,"lo":-2.959831,"d":459,"wp":"en:Bishop's Palace, Kirkwall","ds":"The Bishop's Palace, Kirkwall is a 12th-century palace built at the same time as the adjacent St Magnus Cathedral in the centre of Kirkwall, Orkney, Scotland. It housed the cathedral's first bishop, William the Old of the Norwegian Catholic Church who took his authority from the Archbishop of Nidaros (Trondheim). The ruined structure now looks like a small castle.","wpu":"Bishop's Palace, Kirkwall","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a4/Bishop%27s_Palace_-_Kirkwall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Earl's Palace","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":58.980588,"lo":-2.959045,"d":493,"wp":"en:Earl's Palace, Kirkwall","ds":"The Earl's Palace is a ruined Renaissance-style palace near St Magnus's Cathedral in the centre of Kirkwall, Orkney, Scotland. Built by Patrick, Earl of Orkney, its construction began in 1607 and was largely undertaken via forced labour. Today, the ruins are open to the public.","wpu":"Earl's Palace, Kirkwall","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a6/Earl%27s_Palace%2C_Kirkwall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_82810.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Grain Earth House","g":"sights","k":"yes","la":58.988038,"lo":-2.973921,"d":866,"w":"https://www.historicenvironment.scot/visit-a-place/places/grain-earth-house/"},{"n":"Orcades Hostel","g":"sights","k":"hostel","la":58.981435,"lo":-2.973443,"d":866,"w":"https://www.orcadeshostel.com/","ph":"+44 1856 873 745","wifi":1},{"n":"Kirkwall Youth Hostel","g":"sights","k":"hostel","la":58.975001,"lo":-2.96884,"d":1221,"w":"https://www.hostellingscotland.org.uk/hostels/kirkwall/","ph":"+44 1856 872 243","wifi":1},{"n":"Royal Oak Guest House","g":"sights","k":"guest_house","la":58.973402,"lo":-2.952901,"d":1352,"wifi":1},{"n":"Highland Park Distillery","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":58.969011,"lo":-2.956057,"d":1792,"h":"Apr-Aug,Sep Mo-Fr 10:00-17:00; May-Aug Su 12:00-17:00; Apr,Sep-Mar Sa-Su off; Oct-Mar Mo-Fr 13:00-17:00","w":"http://www.highlandpark.co.uk/","ds":"Highland Park distillery is an Island single malt Scotch whisky distillery located in Kirkwall on the Orkney Islands, Scotland. It is the northernmost single malt Scotch whisky distillery.","wpu":"Highland Park distillery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Highland_Park_Distillery_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2090032.jpg/960px-Highland_Park_Distillery_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2090032.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Highland Park Distillery Visitor Centre","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":58.968186,"lo":-2.955513,"d":1887,"h":"Apr 01-Oct 30 10:00-17:0